{"type":"text","timestamp":1788993505369,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"id":"prt_0885273ba001s5446TjlCRsWAH","messageID":"msg_088526df2001c0MiyYoWJP6uUI","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the test cases and the specification, let me map out what each case should produce:\n\n1. **c01-exhaustive-closed/Verdict**: All cases covered `:placed | :shipped | :lost` → No output (well-formed)\n2. **c02-catchall-open/Open**: Open type (`atom`) with catch-all → No output (well-formed)\n3. **c03-inexhaustive/Missing**: Missing `:lost` case → `switch_inexhaustive`\n4. **c04-unreachable/Shadowed**: `:placed` is duplicated → `unreachable_arm` (arm 3)\n5. **c05-tuple-exhaustive/Decide**: All `(bool, bool, bool)` combinations covered → No output\n6. **c06-tuple-inexhaustive/Partial**: Missing `(false, false)` → `switch_inexhaustive`\n7. **c07-guarded/Retry**: `n when n < 5` rebinds `n` → `rebinding`\n8. **c08-wrong-return/Wrong**: Returns `:gone` (atom) when expecting `int` → `return_not_declared`\n9. **c09-arg-not-accepted/Calls**: Passes `int` to `Tag` which expects `atom` → `arg_not_accepted`\n10. **c10-switch-in-guard/Guarded**: Switch in guard expression → `switch_in_guard`\n11. **c11-unbound-variable/Scopes**: Uses `w` in first arm but only bound in second → `unbound_variable`\n12. **c12-vacuous-arm/Scored**: Pattern `(:pass, n)` not in type `:pass | :fail` → `vacuous_arm`\n13. **c13-unsatisfiable-guard/Graded**: Guard `x > 5 and x < 3` cannot be satisfied → `unsatisfiable_arm_guard`\n\nNow I'll implement the switchcheck tool. Given the complexity of this language, I'll write it in Python:","time":{"start":1788993500090,"end":1788993505358}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788993524243,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"toolu_01CdC3m6oRdsfsCicsK8T9Ub","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nExhaustiveness checker for switch statements.\nImplements the specification from PACKET.md.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Set, Tuple, Optional, Union\nfrom enum import Enum\n\n\nclass TypeKind(Enum):\n    \"\"\"Classification of types for exhaustiveness checking.\"\"\"\n    CLOSED = \"closed\"  # Finite, enumerable cases\n    OPEN = \"open\"      # Unbounded (atom, term, int, etc.)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Type:\n    \"\"\"Represents a type in the language.\"\"\"\n    name: str\n    kind: TypeKind\n    cases: Optional[Set[str]] = None  # For closed types: the enumerated cases\n    \n    def __hash__(self):\n        return hash(self.name)\n    \n    def __eq__(self, other):\n        if not isinstance(other, Type):\n            return False\n        return self.name == other.name\n\n\nclass Pattern:\n    \"\"\"Base class for patterns.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass LiteralPattern(Pattern):\n    \"\"\"Literal value: :atom, 1, etc.\"\"\"\n    value: str\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass NamePattern(Pattern):\n    \"\"\"Variable name binding.\"\"\"\n    name: str\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass WildcardPattern(Pattern):\n    \"\"\"Catch-all: _\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass TuplePattern(Pattern):\n    \"\"\"Tuple pattern: (p1, p2, ...)\"\"\"\n    elements: List[Pattern]\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass ListPattern(Pattern):\n    \"\"\"List pattern: [p1, p2, ..t]\"\"\"\n    elements: List[Pattern]\n    rest_name: Optional[str] = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass RelationalPattern(Pattern):\n    \"\"\"Relational pattern: >= 4, <= 10, == name, etc.\"\"\"\n    op: str  # >=, >, <=, <, ==, !=\n    operand: str  # literal or name\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Arm:\n    \"\"\"A switch arm.\"\"\"\n    pattern: Pattern\n    guard: Optional[str] = None\n    has_switch_in_guard: bool = False\n    returns: Optional[str] = None\n    calls: List[Tuple[str, List[str]]] = None  # List of (func, args)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass SwitchStmt:\n    \"\"\"A switch statement.\"\"\"\n    subject: str  # variable name\n    subject_type: Optional[Type] = None\n    arms: List[Arm] = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Clause:\n    \"\"\"A function clause.\"\"\"\n    name: str\n    params: List[str]\n    patterns: List[Pattern]\n    guard: Optional[str] = None\n    return_type: Optional[str] = None\n\n\nclass Parser:\n    \"\"\"Parses .bs files.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, source: str):\n        self.source = source\n        self.lines = source.split('\\n')\n        self.types: Dict[str, Type] = {}\n        self.functions: Dict[str, Tuple[List[str], str]] = {}  # name -> (param_types, return_type)\n        self.clauses: Dict[str, List[Clause]] = {}  # name -> list of clauses\n        self.errors: List[str] = []\n        \n        # Built-in types\n        self._register_builtin_types()\n    \n    def _register_builtin_types(self):\n        \"\"\"Register built-in open types.\"\"\"\n        for typ in ['atom', 'int', 'term', 'bool', 'bool']:\n            self.types[typ] = Type(typ, TypeKind.OPEN)\n    \n    def parse(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Parse the source. Returns True if parsing succeeded.\"\"\"\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(self.lines):\n            line = self.lines[i].strip()\n            \n            # Skip empty lines and comments\n            if not line or line.startswith('//'):\n                i += 1\n                continue\n            \n            # Type declaration\n            if line.startswith('type '):\n                self._parse_type_def(line)\n                i += 1\n            # Public function signature\n            elif line.startswith('public '):\n                sig_line = line\n                # Collect full signature if it spans multiple lines\n                while i < len(self.lines) - 1 and not sig_line.endswith(')'):\n                    i += 1\n                    sig_line += ' ' + self.lines[i].strip()\n                \n                self._parse_function_sig(sig_line)\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                i += 1\n        \n        return len(self.errors) == 0\n    \n    def _parse_type_def(self, line: str):\n        \"\"\"Parse type definition: type Name = :case1 | :case2\"\"\"\n        match = re.match(r'type\\s+(\\w+)\\s*=\\s*(.*)', line)\n        if match:\n            type_name = match.group(1)\n            cases_str = match.group(2)\n            \n            # Parse cases\n            cases = set()\n            for case in cases_str.split('|'):\n                case = case.strip()\n                if case.startswith(':'):\n                    cases.add(case)\n            \n            self.types[type_name] = Type(type_name, TypeKind.CLOSED, cases)\n    \n    def _parse_function_sig(self, line: str):\n        \"\"\"Parse function signature: public ReturnType Name(ParamType p1, ...)\"\"\"\n        match = re.match(r'public\\s+(\\w+)\\s+(\\w+)\\s*\\((.*)\\)', line)\n        if match:\n            return_type = match.group(1)\n            func_name = match.group(2)\n            params_str = match.group(3)\n            \n            # Parse parameters\n            params = []\n            if params_str.strip():\n                for param in params_str.split(','):\n                    parts = param.strip().split()\n                    if len(parts) >= 2:\n                        params.append(parts[0])  # type\n            \n            self.functions[func_name] = (params, return_type)\n\n\nclass Checker:\n    \"\"\"Main checker for exhaustiveness and other properties.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, source: str):\n        self.source = source\n        self.errors: List[str] = []\n        self.parser = Parser(source)\n        self.lines = source.split('\\n')\n    \n    def check(self) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Run all checks and return diagnostic tags.\"\"\"\n        self.parser.parse()\n        self._analyze_switches()\n        self._analyze_scopes()\n        return sorted(self.errors)\n    \n    def _analyze_switches(self):\n        \"\"\"Analyze switch statements for exhaustiveness and arm validity.\"\"\"\n        for i, line in enumerate(self.lines):\n            if 'switch' in line:\n                self._check_switch_at_line(i)\n    \n    def _analyze_scopes(self):\n        \"\"\"Analyze variable scopes.\"\"\"\n        for i, line in enumerate(self.lines):\n            if '=>' in line and '(' in line:\n                self._check_arm_scope(i)\n    \n    def _check_switch_at_line(self, line_idx: int):\n        \"\"\"Check a switch statement starting at line_idx.\"\"\"\n        # Stub implementation\n        pass\n    \n    def _check_arm_scope(self, line_idx: int):\n        \"\"\"Check variable scopes in an arm.\"\"\"\n        # Stub implementation\n        pass\n\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        sys.stderr.write(\"Usage: switchcheck <path-to-.bs-file>\\n\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n    \n    filepath = sys.argv[1]\n    \n    try:\n        with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n            source = f.read()\n    except Exception as e:\n        sys.stderr.write(f\"Error reading file: {e}\\n\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n    \n    checker = Checker(source)\n    errors = checker.check()\n    \n    for error in errors:\n        print(error)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","time":{"start":1788993524093,"end":1788993524212}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_088528856001NIL7Au6XS9ue9S","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","messageID":"msg_088526df2001c0MiyYoWJP6uUI"}}
