{"type":"text","timestamp":1788993975147,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"id":"prt_08859aee8001JJ6pbUmtnuI7XM","messageID":"msg_08859aa350013wtWMYmax9pA94","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","type":"text","text":"So the clause is at line 2 and the switch is also at line 2. When we collect the switch and call `_analyze_switch` with `line_idx=2`, we need to find clause params from line 2 itself. But the issue is that clause params are extracted while parsing, and they're stored by line number. Let me verify the parsing works:","time":{"start":1788993973992,"end":1788993975145}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788993979500,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01AuKTpAVunmKQFPysfnW6ot","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45 && python3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport re\n\nsource = open('cases/c06-tuple-inexhaustive/Partial/in.bs').read()\nlines = source.split('\\n')\n\n# Simulate parsing\nclause_params = {}\n\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    line_stripped = line.strip()\n    if re.match(r'\\w+\\s*\\(', line_stripped):\n        m = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\s*\\((.*?)\\)', line_stripped)\n        if m:\n            func_name = m.group(1)\n            params_str = m.group(2)\n            \n            # This matches the clause\n            params_list = [p.strip() for p in params_str.split(',')]\n            \n            # We have param_types = ['bool', 'bool'] from function\n            param_types = ['bool', 'bool']\n            \n            mapping = dict(zip(params_list, param_types))\n            clause_params[i] = mapping\n            \n            print(f\"Line {i}: clause {func_name} -> mapping {mapping}\")\n\n# Now when analyzing switch at line 2:\nswitch_line_idx = 2\nrecent_clause = None\nfor line_idx in sorted(clause_params.keys(), reverse=True):\n    if line_idx < switch_line_idx + 1:  # <= not <\n        recent_clause = line_idx\n        break\n\nprint(f\"\\nFinding clause for switch at line {switch_line_idx}\")\nprint(f\"Sorted clause lines: {sorted(clause_params.keys())}\")\nprint(f\"Recent clause: {recent_clause}\")\nPYEOF\n"},"output":"zsh:1: can't create temp file for here document: operation not permitted\n","metadata":{"output":"zsh:1: can't create temp file for here document: operation not permitted\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45 && python3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport re\n\nsource = open('cases/c06-tuple-inexhaustive/Partial/in.bs').read()\nlines = source.split('\\n')\n\n# Simulate parsing\nclause_params = {}\n\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    line_stripped = line.strip()\n    if re.match(r'\\w+\\s*\\(', line_stripped):\n        m = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\s*\\((.*?)\\)', line_stripped)\n        if m:\n            func_name = m.group(1)\n            params_str = m.group(2)\n            \n            # This matches the clause\n            params_list = [p.strip() for p in params_str.split(',')]\n            \n            # We have param_types = ['bool', 'bool'] from function\n            param_types = ['bool', 'bool']\n            \n            mapping = dict(zip(params_list, param_types))\n            clause_params[i] = mapping\n            \n            print(f\"Line {i}: clause {func_name} -> mapping {mapping}\")\n\n# Now when analyzing switch at line 2:\nswitch_line_idx = 2\nrecent_clause = None\nfor line_idx in sorted(clause_params.keys(), reverse=True):\n    if line_idx < switch_line_idx + 1:  # <= not <\n        recent_clause = line_idx\n        break\n\nprint(f\"\\nFinding clause for switch at line {switch_line_idx}\")\nprint(f\"Sorted clause lines: {sorted(clause_params.keys())}\")\nprint(f\"Recent clause: {recent_clause}\")\nPYEOF\n","time":{"start":1788993979447,"end":1788993979450}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_08859b36a001Yj7CSbDnhR7BeV","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","messageID":"msg_08859aa350013wtWMYmax9pA94"}}
