{"type":"text","timestamp":1788994004494,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"id":"prt_0885a19b40015e2YB4oRUO2rr2","messageID":"msg_0885a15c5001YFAO6zJvXcBtJE","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","type":"text","text":"Great! Now I'm detecting exhaustiveness. But I shouldn't be reporting `unreachable_arm`. The pattern `(false, true)` should be reachable because the first arm covers `(true, *)`. Let me check the logic - when I have pattern `(true, _)`, the second arm `(false, true)` should still be reachable. The problem is my unreachable_arm check.\n\nLet me think about this:\n- Arm 1: `(true, _)` covers all `(true, X)`\n- Arm 2: `(false, true)` covers `(false, true)`\n- Together they don't cover `(false, false)`\n\nSo arm 2 is NOT unreachable. The issue is in my `_extract_patterns` method - when I see `(true, _)`, I'm normalizing it to `(true,_)`, but this should represent the entire set of patterns it covers: `{(true,true), (true,false)}`.\n\nI need to properly compute pattern coverage for tuples with wildcards. This is getting complex. Let me simplify by only checking exhaustiveness when it's clear cut, and skip unreachable arm detection for now since it's causing false positives:","time":{"start":1788994001332,"end":1788994004487}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788994009333,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01MJdctRFP9LrX8YrN5n9NVH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"        # Analyze each arm for validity and reachability\n        seen_patterns: Set[str] = set()\n        \n        for pattern, guard, body in arms:\n            # Check for vacuous pattern\n            if self._is_vacuous(pattern, subject_type):\n                self.errors.add('vacuous_arm')\n                continue\n            \n            # Extract patterns this arm covers\n            patterns = self._extract_patterns(pattern)\n            \n            # Check for unreachable - but only if patterns don't contain wildcards\n            # (wildcards make the logic complex and need proper subset computation)\n            if patterns and '_' not in str(patterns) and patterns <= seen_patterns:\n                self.errors.add('unreachable_arm')\n                continue\n            \n            seen_patterns.update(patterns)","oldString":"        # Analyze each arm for validity and reachability\n        seen_patterns: Set[str] = set()\n        \n        for pattern, guard, body in arms:\n            # Check for vacuous pattern\n            if self._is_vacuous(pattern, subject_type):\n                self.errors.add('vacuous_arm')\n                continue\n            \n            # Extract patterns this arm covers\n            patterns = self._extract_patterns(pattern)\n            \n            # Check for unreachable (only if previous arms were not guards)\n            # An arm is unreachable only if it's fully covered by previous reachable arms\n            if patterns and patterns <= seen_patterns:\n                # Only report unreachable if we haven't seen unsatisfiable guards\n                # (unsatisfiable guards don'