{"type":"text","timestamp":1788994019097,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"id":"prt_0885a530e001eEXBi2jZNy5QOH","messageID":"msg_0885a4eeb001gPbIIfHVpginea","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","type":"text","text":"This is a 3-tuple, not a 2-tuple. My generation only handles 2-tuples. Let me add 3-tuple generation (which I already have). The issue is that my `_extract_patterns` isn't computing the full coverage properly.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. For patterns with wildcards like `(true, _, _)`, I need to determine what cases it covers. The pattern `(true, _, _)` covers:\n- `(true, true, true)`\n- `(true, true, false)`\n- `(true, false, true)`\n- `(true, false, false)`\n\nThen `(false, true, _)` covers:\n- `(false, true, true)`\n- `(false, true, false)`\n\nAnd `(false, false, false)` and `(false, false, true)` cover the remaining cases.\n\nI need a smarter pattern matcher. For now, let me try a simpler approach: count how many possible patterns each arm covers and check if they sum to 8 (for 3 bools):","time":{"start":1788994016014,"end":1788994019085}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788994023479,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01PdUnrpH6q1gqf7Ym4RVFw7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"    def _extract_patterns(self, pattern: str) -> Set[str]:\n        \"\"\"Extract literal patterns from pattern string.\"\"\"\n        patterns = set()\n        \n        pattern = pattern.strip()\n        \n        # Wildcard\n        if pattern == '_':\n            patterns.add('_')\n            return patterns\n        \n        # Tuple pattern - need to compute what it covers\n        if pattern.startswith('(') and pattern.endswith(')'):\n            # For now, just normalize it\n            # Later we'll need to compute coverage\n            normalized = self._normalize_tuple(pattern)\n            \n            # If it has wildcards, mark with *\n            if '_' in normalized:\n                patterns.add(normalized + '*')\n            else:\n                patterns.add(normalized)\n        elif ':' in pattern:\n            # Atom patterns\n            for m in re.finditer(r':\\w+', pattern):\n                patterns.add(m.group())\n        else:\n            # Name binding treats as wildcard\n            patterns.add('_')\n        \n        return patterns","oldString":"    def _extract_patterns(self, pattern: str) -> Set[str]:\n        \"\"\"Extract literal patterns from pattern string.\"\"\"\n        patterns = set()\n        \n        pattern = pattern.strip()\n        \n        # Wildcard\n        if pattern == '_':\n            patterns.add('_')\n            return patterns\n        \n        # Tuple pattern\n        if pattern.startswith('(') and pattern.endswith(')'):\n            # Normalize for comparison\n            patterns.add(self._normalize_tuple(pattern))\n        elif ':' in pattern:\n            # Atom patterns\n            for m in re.finditer(r':\\w+', pattern):\n                patterns.add(m.group())\n        else:\n            # Name binding treats as wildcard\n            patterns.add('_')\n        \n        return patterns"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -350,12 +350,19 @@\n if pattern == '_':\n     patterns.add('_')\n     return patterns\n \n-# Tuple pattern\n+# Tuple pattern - need to compute what it covers\n if pattern.startswith('(') and pattern.endswith(')'):\n-    # Normalize for comparison\n-    patterns.add(self._normalize_tuple(pattern))\n+    # For now, just normalize it\n+    # Later we'll need to compute coverage\n+    normalized = self._normalize_tuple(pattern)\n+    \n+    # If it has wildcards, mark with *\n+    if '_' in normalized:\n+        patterns.add(normalized + '*')\n+    else:\n+        patterns.add(normalized)\n elif ':' in pattern:\n     # Atom patterns\n     for m in re.finditer(r':\\w+', pattern):\n         patterns.add(m.group())\n","filediff":{"file":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","patch":"Index: /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -350,12 +350,19 @@\n if pattern == '_':\n     patterns.add(