{"type":"text","timestamp":1788994112626,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"id":"prt_0885b8db1001DDY3vg8X8c7bw0","messageID":"msg_0885b88c6001tELsDxhl2qLPa4","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Implement `switchcheck`: a command-line tool that analyzes `.bs` files to detect pattern matching errors in switch statements\n- Tool must print lowercase diagnostic tags (one per line) for specific errors; well-formed programs print nothing\n\n## Important Details\n- Hard rules: work only in working directory `/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/`, do not read files outside it, do not modify `cases/` directory\n- Output contract: only these 9 tags permitted: `switch_inexhaustive`, `unreachable_arm`, `vacuous_arm`, `unsatisfiable_arm_guard`, `rebinding`, `unbound_variable`, `return_not_declared`, `arg_not_accepted`, `switch_in_guard`\n- Deliverable: executable `./switchcheck <path-to-.bs-file>` with shebang, runnable directly\n- Language has: type definitions (`type State = :placed | :shipped`), closed/open types, function signatures (`public atom Func(Type param)`), clauses with patterns, switch statements with guards, tuples\n- Clause heads `Route(o, p) ->` establish parameter bindings that map to function signature types; e.g., `o` gets type of first param\n- Multi-line switches must be collected as complete text before parsing\n- Pattern extraction must handle: atoms (`:name`), tuples `(pattern, pattern)`, wildcards `_`, name bindings, tuples of bools generate all 2^n combinations\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Parser for type definitions, function signatures, clause heads\n- Basic exhaustiveness checking for closed types (single variables and tuples)\n- Unreachable arm detection (duplicate literal patterns)\n- `rebinding` detection (pattern name matches parameter name)\n- `unbound_variable` detection (with fix to not treat atom suffixes as identifiers)\n- `return_not_declared` detection (type mismatch in return values)\n- `switch_in_guard` detection (switch appearing after `when` keyword)\n- `unsatisfiable_arm_guard` detection (x > 5 and x < 3 style contradictions)\n- Multi-line switch collection (via brace counting)\n- Tuple type inference for subjects like `(o, p)` with bool parameters\n- Tuple normalization for pattern comparison `(true,  _)` → `(true,_)`\n- Test case 01–05, 08, 10, 11: mostly working\n\n### Active\n- Fixing false positive `unreachable_arm` errors when:\n  - Guard is unsatisfiable (should not count toward coverage)\n  - Pattern is rebinding (treated as wildcard, but still checking reachability)\n- Implementing `vacuous_arm` detection (e.g., tuple pattern against atom-only type)\n- Implementing `arg_not_accepted` detection (function call with wrong arg type)\n- Ensuring clause parameter mappings propagate correctly to subject type inference\n\n### Blocked\n- c06 (tuple inexhaustive): tuple pattern normalization works, but exhaustiveness not triggered; likely clause_params not being found or passed correctly\n- c07 (rebinding): reports both `rebinding` ✓ and spurious `unreachable_arm`\n- c09 (arg_not_accepted): reports `unreachable_arm` instead; likely arm coverage logic interfering with call checking\n- c12 (vacuous arm): no detection; need to verify vacuous pattern logic for `(:pass, n)` against type `:pass | :fail`\n- c13 (unsatisfiable guard): reports both `unsatisfiable_arm_guard` ✓ and spurious `unreachable_arm`\n\n## Next Move\n1. Debug clause_params assignment: verify `_parse_clause_head()` is called and that `clause_params[line_idx]` is set before switch analysis in c06\n2. Fix unreachable_arm logic: skip reporting if any previous arm has unsatisfiable guard or if arm is vacuous\n3. Trace c09 to confirm `Big(m)` call detection; ensure `_infer_type()` handles parameter variables correctly\n4. Verify `_is_vacuous()` logic for tuple patterns against non-tuple types\n5. Test all cases again; compare output to expected per test case mapping\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck`: main implementation (Python3 with shebang)\n- `/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md`: language specification (read-only reference)\n- `/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/cases/c0[1-13]-*/*/in.bs`: 13 test cases with expected error tags in directory names","time":{"start":1788994096561,"end":1788994112583}}}
