{"type":"text","timestamp":1788994225008,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"id":"prt_0885d6dc1001ugeoEwMsVPBIEq","messageID":"msg_0885d68f7001zv2sKoG314VGAv","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","type":"text","text":"The error is in the guard `Big(m)` where `m` is bound in the pattern. But `Big` expects an `int`, and `m` comes from the pattern which is bound to an `int` value (from `Check(n)` where `n` is an int). Wait, let me re-read:\n\nThe pattern is `m when Big(m)`. So `m` is a name binding (pattern variable). Since the subject is `n` (which has type `int`), `m` gets type `int`. Then the guard calls `Big(m)` where `Big` expects an `int`. So that should be fine!\n\nWait, let me re-read the spec. The issue might be that `Big` returns `bool`, but we're in a guard context. Let me check the spec:\n\nLooking back at the PACKET.md reference, a guard should be a boolean expression. So `Big(m)` which returns `bool` should be fine. But the error is `arg_not_accepted`, not something about the guard return type.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The pattern is `m`, which has an implicit type constraint. But what value is `m` matching? The switch subject is `n`, which has type `int`. So `m` is bound to an `int` value. Then `Big(m)` passes an `int` to `Big`, which expects an `int`. This should be fine!\n\nUnless... let me re-read the file. Is there something else?\n\nActually, wait. Maybe the issue is that `Tag(m)` in the body is being called. `Tag` expects an `atom`, but `m` is an `int`. That would be `arg_not_accepted` on the body, not the pattern!\n\nLet me check if the code checks the body for function calls:","time":{"start":1788994219457,"end":1788994224989}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788994225290,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01EoivdZTyCRCYz9JyfHKPT7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -A 30 \"_check_calls\" /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck | head -40"},"output":"        self._check_calls()\n        \n        return sorted(self.errors)\n    \n    def _check_switches(self):\n        \"\"\"Check switch statements.\"\"\"\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(self.lines):\n            if 'switch {' in self.lines[i]:\n                switch_text = self._collect_switch(i)\n                self._analyze_switch(switch_text, i)\n                i += switch_text.count('\\n')\n            i += 1\n    \n    def _collect_switch(self, start_idx: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Collect multi-line switch.\"\"\"\n        lines = [self.lines[start_idx]]\n        i = start_idx + 1\n        brace_depth = lines[0].count('{') - lines[0].count('}')\n        \n        while i < len(self.lines) and brace_depth > 0:\n            lines.append(self.lines[i])\n            brace_depth += self.lines[i].count('{') - self.lines[i].count('}')\n            i += 1\n        \n        return '\\n'.join(lines)\n    \n    def _analyze_switch(self, switch_text: str, line_idx: int):\n        \"\"\"Analyze a switch statement.\"\"\"\n        # Extract subject (appears between -> and switch)\n        m = re.search(r'->\\s*(.+?)\\s+switch\\s*\\{', switch_text)\n--\n    def _check_calls(self):\n        \"\"\"Check function call arguments.\"\"\"\n        for func_name, (param_types, _, _) in self.functions.items():\n            for line in self.lines:\n                if '=>' not in line:\n                    continue\n                \n                m = re.search(rf'{func_name}\\s*\\(([^)]*)\\)', line)\n","metadata":{"output":"        self._check_calls()\n        \n        return sorted(self.errors)\n    \n    def _check_switches(self):\n        \"\"\"Check switch statements.\"\"\"\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(self.lines):\n            if 'switch {' in self.lines[i]:\n                switch_text = self._collect_switch(i)\n                self._analyze_switch(switch_text, i)\n                i += switch_text.count('\\n')\n            i += 1\n    \n    def _collect_switch(self, start_idx: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Collect multi-line switch.\"\"\"\n        lines = [self.lines[start_idx]]\n        i = start_idx + 1\n        brace_depth = lines[0].count('{') - lines[0].count('}')\n        \n        while i < len(self.lines) and brace_depth > 0:\n            lines.append(self.lines[i])\n            brace_depth += self.lines[i].count('{') - self.lines[i].count('}')\n            i += 1\n        \n        return '\\n'.join(lines)\n    \n    def _analyze_switch(self, switch_text: str, line_idx: int):\n        \"\"\"Analyze a switch statement.\"\"\"\n        # Extract subject (appears between -> and switch)\n        m = re.search(r'->\\s*(.+?)\\s+switch\\s*\\{', switch_text)\n--\n    def _check_calls(self):\n        \"\"\"Check function call arguments.\"\"\"\n        for func_name, (param_types, _, _) in self.functions.items():\n            for line in self.lines:\n                if '=>' not in line:\n                    continue\n                \n                m = re.search(rf'{func_name}\\s*\\(([^)]*)\\)', line)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -A 30 \"_check_calls\" /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck | head -40","time":{"start":1788994225232,"end":1788994225235}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_0885d836d0014HtVSpM0XwZJhN","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","messageID":"msg_0885d68f7001zv2sKoG314VGAv"}}
