{"type":"text","timestamp":1788994344158,"sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","part":{"id":"prt_0885f3685001KPABkHXD8Y4rDE","messageID":"msg_0885f324c001Wfc4BXivMsxpsS","sessionID":"ses_f77ade3dcffeRFa5D7H8svAwTg","type":"text","text":"Excellent! The switchcheck tool is complete and working. Let me create a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI'"'"'ve successfully implemented **switchcheck**, a command-line tool that analyzes `.bs` files to detect pattern matching errors in switch statements.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n\n1. **Exhaustiveness Checking** (`switch_inexhaustive`)\n   - For closed types (enums), verifies all cases are covered\n   - Handles tuple patterns with wildcards using Cartesian product expansion\n   - Correctly accounts for satisfiable guards when computing coverage\n\n2. **Unreachable Arm Detection** (`unreachable_arm`)\n   - Identifies duplicate literal patterns that can never be reached\n   - Skips checking when patterns contain wildcards (to avoid false positives)\n\n3. **Rebinding Detection** (`rebinding`)\n   - Flags when a pattern variable shadows a function parameter\n\n4. **Unbound Variable Detection** (`unbound_variable`)\n   - Identifies variables in switch bodies that aren'"'"'t bound by the pattern or parameters\n   - Excludes function names from the error\n\n5. **Return Type Mismatch** (`return_not_declared`)\n   - Detects when switch arm body returns wrong type for the function\n\n6. **Vacuous Pattern Detection** (`vacuous_arm`)\n   - Identifies impossible patterns (e.g., atom pattern against non-atom type)\n\n7. **Unsatisfiable Guard Detection** (`unsatisfiable_arm_guard`)\n   - Finds contradictory guard conditions like `x > 5 and x < 3`\n\n8. **Switch in Guard Detection** (`switch_in_guard`)\n   - Flags when a switch statement appears in a guard (when clause)\n\n9. **Argument Type Mismatch** (`arg_not_accepted`)\n   - Checks function calls in switch bodies have correct argument types\n   - Infers pattern variable types from subject declarations\n\n### Architecture\n\n- **Parser**: Extracts types, functions, clauses, and switch statements\n- **Multi-line collection**: Handles switches spanning multiple lines via brace counting\n- **Arm extraction**: Line-by-line parsing of switch arms with pattern/guard/body separation\n- **Type inference**: Tracks variable types through clause parameters and pattern bindings\n- **Validation**: Nine distinct error checks applied to switch statements\n\n### Test Results\n\nAll 13 test cases passing:\n- ✓ c01: Exhaustive closed type\n- ✓ c02: Open type (no exhaustiveness check)\n- ✓ c03: Inexhaustive switch\n- ✓ c04: Unreachable arm\n- ✓ c05: Tuple exhaustive\n- ✓ c06: Tuple inexhaustive  \n- ✓ c07: Rebinding error\n- ✓ c08: Wrong return type\n- ✓ c09: Wrong argument type\n- ✓ c10: Switch in guard\n- ✓ c11: Unbound variable\n- ✓ c12: Vacuous arm\n- ✓ c13: Unsatisfiable guard","time":{"start":1788994336389,"end":1788994344147}}}
