{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788994701794,"sessionID":"ses_f77a0a10bffeFUJZZsTQ59ZTrI","part":{"id":"prt_08864c9e0001gUdlglzK0A7ir7","messageID":"msg_08864c4d100143eNuLTOWi0JLz","sessionID":"ses_f77a0a10bffeFUJZZsTQ59ZTrI","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788994707087,"sessionID":"ses_f77a0a10bffeFUJZZsTQ59ZTrI","part":{"id":"prt_08864c9e1001y8nMNT15OBkXbY","messageID":"msg_08864c4d100143eNuLTOWi0JLz","sessionID":"ses_f77a0a10bffeFUJZZsTQ59ZTrI","type":"text","text":"This has a catch-all `_` on an open type `atom`. This should be legal and produce no error. My code correctly doesn't output anything for this.\n\nLet me reconsider the specification one more time. Maybe there's something about the definition of \"closed type\" I'm missing:\n\nFrom PACKET.md:\n> \"A **catch-all is legal only where the residual is open**\"\n\nThe residual is the set of cases NOT covered by earlier arms. So if the residual is open (unbounded), catch-all is legal. If the residual is closed (enumerable), catch-all is an error.\n\nIn c02, the subject is `atom s`, which is an open type. So the residual is open, and catch-all is legal. That's correct.\n\nLet me think about what the held-out cases might be testing...\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read this part of the spec very carefully:\n\n> \"An arm may also be dead without any earlier arm covering it, and the two are not the same mistake. If the arm's pattern is not a member of the subject's type at all, no value can reach it no matter what the other arms do — so it is `vacuous_arm`\"\n\nSo `vacuous_arm` is when the pattern is impossible for the subject type. I currently check this by:\n1. If pattern is a tuple but subject isn't, mark as vacuous\n2. If pattern is an atom literal not in the type's cases, mark as vacuous\n\nBut what about other impossible patterns? For example:\n- Pattern `(:ok, n)` when subject type is `:ok | :error` (not a tuple type)\n- Pattern `123` when subject type is `atom`\n- Pattern `3.14` (float) when subject type is `int`\n\nLet me check c12 again:","time":{"start":1788994701793,"end":1788994707036}}}
