{"type":"text","timestamp":1788994851257,"sessionID":"ses_f77a0a10bffeFUJZZsTQ59ZTrI","part":{"id":"prt_088670235001DOvvdh1vjMQNKn","messageID":"msg_08866fc29001NPs2Xq6wQiq03p","sessionID":"ses_f77a0a10bffeFUJZZsTQ59ZTrI","type":"text","text":"Wait, but this might mark all arms after a catch-all as unreachable, even if the catch-all is itself legal (on an open type). Let me reconsider...\n\nActually, from the spec example:\n\n```csharp\nWhich(a) -> a switch {\n    _  => :any,\n    :x => :ex\n}\n```\n\nThe comment says:\n\n> \"— *arm 2 of this switch in `Which` is unreachable; every value it matches is matched by an earlier arm.*\"\n\nSo yes, if there's a catch-all before another arm, that arm is unreachable. But we should still report this as an error, regardless of whether the catch-all is \"legal\" (which it's not on closed types anyway).\n\nBut wait - let me check c04 again to see if it has this issue:\n\n```csharp\nDescribe(s) -> s switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone,\n    :placed  => :again\n}\n```\n\nThis has `:placed` twice. My current code would mark the second as unreachable, which is correct.\n\nLet me test to make sure I haven't broken anything:","time":{"start":1788994847285,"end":1788994851216}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788994852976,"sessionID":"ses_f77a0a10bffeFUJZZsTQ59ZTrI","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01L1yWrkeatZn97TxWPP8xhP","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45 && for case in cases/c*/*/in.bs; do cname=$(echo $case | sed 's|cases/||; s|/.*||'); result=$(./switchcheck \"$case\" 2>&1); echo \"$cname: $result\"; done"},"output":"c01-exhaustive-closed: \nc02-catchall-open: \nc03-inexhaustive: switch_inexhaustive\nc04-unreachable: unreachable_arm\nc05-tuple-exhaustive: \nc06-tuple-inexhaustive: switch_inexhaustive\nc07-guarded: rebinding\nc08-wrong-return: return_not_declared\nc09-arg-not-accepted: arg_not_accepted\nc10-switch-in-guard: switch_in_guard\nc11-unbound-variable: unbound_variable\nc12-vacuous-arm: vacuous_arm\nc13-unsatisfiable-guard: unsatisfiable_arm_guard\n","metadata":{"output":"c01-exhaustive-closed: \nc02-catchall-open: \nc03-inexhaustive: switch_inexhaustive\nc04-unreachable: unreachable_arm\nc05-tuple-exhaustive: \nc06-tuple-inexhaustive: switch_inexhaustive\nc07-guarded: rebinding\nc08-wrong-return: return_not_declared\nc09-arg-not-accepted: arg_not_accepted\nc10-switch-in-guard: switch_in_guard\nc11-unbound-variable: unbound_variable\nc12-vacuous-arm: vacuous_arm\nc13-unsatisfiable-guard: unsatisfiable_arm_guard\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-09-round3/copilot-haiku45 && for case in cases/c*/*/in.bs; do cname=$(echo $case | sed 's|cases/||; s|/.*||'); result=$(./switchcheck \"$case\" 2>&1); echo \"$cname: $result\"; done","time":{"start":1788994852946,"end":1788994852949}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_088671195001a25bAbpeBJj0ul","sessionID":"ses_f77a0a10bffeFUJZZsTQ59ZTrI","messageID":"msg_08866fc29001NPs2Xq6wQiq03p"}}
